# Build-context exclusions for every image in docker-compose.yml.
#
# Both Dockerfiles use the REPO ROOT as their build context (the frontend needs
# package.json / pnpm-workspace.yaml / pnpm-lock.yaml, the backend needs
# pyproject.toml / uv.lock — all of which live here, not in apps/*). Without
# this file every `docker build` would upload node_modules/, .venv/ and .next/
# to the daemon, and — worse — a `COPY . .` would bake host-built artefacts
# into the image, where a Linux container would try to execute macOS/WSL
# binaries and a stale .next/ would shadow a fresh build.
#
# Style: deny-list, not allow-list. An allow-list silently drops new source
# directories as the repo grows; a missing deny entry only costs build time.

# --- Dependency trees: always reinstalled inside the image from the lockfiles.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.venv/
**/.venv/
.pnpm-store/

# --- Build output and tool caches.
.next/
**/.next/
out/
**/out/
*.tsbuildinfo
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# --- VCS and agent/editor state. `.git` in particular is large and, for the
# frontend image, its absence is load-bearing: lefthook's postinstall detects
# no repository and no-ops (it also swallows failures under CI=true).
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Secrets. Nothing here today (the first .env lands in Phase 1 with
# gitleaks), but an image must never be able to absorb one by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Docs, plans and phase scaffolding: not needed to build or run any image.
# README.md is deliberately NOT excluded: apps/api and packages/database both
# declare `readme = "../../README.md"`, and their build backend reads it while
# resolving metadata, so dropping it breaks `uv sync`.
#
# `prompts/` is deliberately NOT excluded either, as of Phase 3. It was excluded
# while it held only a .gitkeep; it now holds the prompt versions the backend
# loads at runtime (docs/SPEC.md §12), so an image without it starts fine and
# then fails on the first summary with a FileNotFoundError.
docs/
plans/
tests/
CLAUDE.md
Makefile
lefthook.yml
docker-compose.yml

# --- OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
